# Malloy for Software Engineers

For software engineers building data-driven experiences with Malloy—analytics features, internal tools, AI-powered apps, or anywhere you need consistent, reusable data.

## The Journey

### 1. Model Your Data
Build semantic models that encode the meaning of your data.

- **[Model Your Data](modeling/modeling.malloynb)** - Define sources, add measures/dimensions/joins, create views
- [Troubleshooting](modeling/troubleshooting.malloynb) - Fix common modeling issues

### 2. Publish Your Models
Deploy semantic models via Malloy Publisher.

- **[Publish Your Models](publishing/publishing.malloynb)** - Deploy locally or to production with Docker

### 3. Build Consumption Experiences
Enable analysts, apps, and AI agents to use your models.

- [REST API](consuming/rest_api.malloynb) - Build custom applications
- [Publisher SDK](consuming/publisher_sdk.malloynb) - Embed analytics in React apps (includes [Explorer](consuming/explorer.malloynb) component)
- [MCP for AI Agents](consuming/mcp_agents.malloynb) - Integrate with Claude and other AI

### 4. Transform Data (Optional)
Materialize large tables or clean messy data before modeling.

- [Transform Data](transform/transform_data.malloynb) - Use CLI & MalloySQL for performance optimization and data prep

## Quick Start Options

**New to Malloy?** Start with [Model Your Data](modeling/modeling.malloynb) - you'll have a working model in 15 minutes.

**Ready to deploy?** Skip to [Publish Your Models](publishing/publishing.malloynb).

## Prerequisites

- Access to your data (BigQuery, Snowflake, Postgres, DuckDB, or files)
- [VS Code with the Malloy extension](../setup/extension.malloynb) (for modeling)
